{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310651,"nonce":"YRqUsKnRkXWaleSfkmDg2WYbdPU=","title":"drop_analysis.mark_escaping only matched bare Variable, no-op'd for composite exprs — fixed to recurse into ...","message":"`compiler/src/ir/drop_analysis.rs::mark_escaping` previously matched\nonly `HirExprKind::Variable { symbol }` and silently no-op'd for\nevery other expression kind. Effect: variables flowing through\ncomposite expressions at call/return sites were not marked\nescaping, so the drop point analyzer's \"last use\" could fire mid\nloop body when a later use was wrapped in a field/index access.\n\n**Symptom shape**:\n- `obj.method(other.field)` — `other` not marked escaping; its\n  recorded last use could be an earlier direct reference.\n- `f(arr[i])` — neither `arr` nor `i` marked escaping at this call.\n- `result.set(info.name, tensor)` — `info` not marked escaping\n  here (only `tensor` was); `info`'s lifetime is decided by other\n  uses elsewhere in the loop body.\n\n**Fix**: `mark_escaping` now recurses into `Field`, `Index`,\n`Cast`, `Unary`, `Binary`, `Call` (callee + every arg), `New`,\n`Array`, and `If` (both branches). Each leaf `Variable` still\nflips on `self.escaping.insert(symbol)`. The ordinary\n`analyze_expr` recursion continues to record last-use as before\n— the two passes serve different purposes and don't conflict.\n\n**How to apply**: Whenever you add a new `HirExprKind` variant\nthat can syntactically contain variables, also add it to\n`mark_escaping` so they survive the \"last use\" drop.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_cleanup_scopes_frees_captures]] (prior UAF in\ncleanup_all_scopes, fixed in 64d98ea).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_mark_escaping_incomplete` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}